{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses","id":1029550,"title":"What happens when a Paradox Condition Lapses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T04:40:04-08:00","id":1029550,"title":"What happens when a Paradox Condition Lapses?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Paradox Condition is allowed to lapse, the Abyss enters the mage\u2019s Pattern. While the Abyss is part of the mage\u2019s Pattern, it appears in her Nimbus. Every spell she casts is tainted by the Abyss and gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell. Conditions that resolve this way grant an Arcane Beat. At this point, the only way for the mage to remove the taint from her Pattern is to Scour it out, similar to Pattern Scouring for Mana as described on p. 87. <b>Removing a Paradox Condition in this manner</b> deals a single point of lethal damage to the mage, but she does not gain Mana from the Scouring. </div> </div> </div>The text implies that the Paradox Condition lapsing removes it, and replaces it with this Abyssal Taint effect. However, the bolded part of the text implies that the Condition actually remains until you scour it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resolution: </b>An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. <br /> <b>Arcane Beat: </b>Gain an Arcane Beat when this Condition lapses. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resolution: </b>The mage successfully casts a spell that does not risk Paradox, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. <br /> <b>Arcane Beat: </b>Gain an Arcane Beat when this Condition lapses. </div> </div> </div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resolution: </b>The mage fully contains a Paradox, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. <br /> <b>Arcane Beat: </b>Gain an Arcane Beat when this Condition lapses. </div> </div> </div>Note that the 'Beat' section exists for things that give you a Beat but don't resolve the Condition. Its presence implies that the Condition persists somehow after lapsing, despite lapsing being a resolution Criteria. Either the presence of this section must be an error, or lapsing causing resolution must be an error.<br /> <br /> Which of these cases is true?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Allowing a Condition to lapse resolves it. </b> The presence of the Arcane Beat section on the following Conditions is an error, and the bolded statement above is referring to 'removing abyssal taint from a lapsed Paradox Condition', not 'removing a Paradox Condition'.</li> <li><b>Allowing a Condition to lapse grants an Arcane Beat, but does not resolve it.</b> The mage continues to suffer under the condition, and the Abyssal Taint effect, until they scour the Condition as described above, resolving it.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T04:57:27-08:00","id":1029554,"title":"","content":"The Condition persists as Abyssal Taint and forces a aparadox die on your spells, but no longer maintains its original effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T09:27:14-08:00","id":1029630,"title":"","content":"I think 1 is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:33:27-08:00","id":1029761,"title":"","content":"Then, each condition lists scouring as a possible method for removal.<br /> <br /> But,the intro paragraph contradicts it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each one has two resolution mechanics. The first requires the character to actively accept the negative consequence of the Paradox, and the other is to allow the Paradox to lapse. </div> </div> </div>Each condition lists <i>three</i> resolution methods: Lapsing, Scouring, or the natural resolution.<br /> <br /> This section is such a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:01:05-08:00","id":1029780,"title":"","content":"Scouring happens after Lapsing which isn't a Resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:12:31-08:00","id":1029916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029780#post1029780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scouring happens after Lapsing which isn't a Resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>But scouring and lapsing are both listed as resolutions for the base Condition.<br /> <br /> At this point, it seems like there are two very different ways this was originally meant to be handled, and they've been mashed together through editing, rendering the whole thing incomprehensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-11-2017, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T23:19:49-08:00","id":1029936,"title":"","content":"My reading is that contradictions stemming from the Condition writeup framework should be disregarded in favor of the intro paragraph proper \u2014 Scouring isn't framed as a resolution method, lapsing is specifically contrasted with resolution and, per the book's section on Conditions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When your character resolves a Condition, take a Beat. If a Condition has a natural time limit and then fades away, don\u2019t take a Beat \u2014 just waiting the Condition out isn\u2019t enough to count as resolving it. </div> </div> </div>You get a regular Beat for actively accepting the negative consequences of the Paradox or an Arcane Beat for letting the Paradox lapse after spending the Wisdom-determined duration without taking action to resolve it; if the Condition lapses, it goes away and leaves behind a consequence that cannot be represented with a Condition without specifying that its resolution does not grant a Beat.<br /> <br /> So, to use Abyssal Nimbus as an example, the fields would more clearly read:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resolution:</b> An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest.<br /> <b>Arcane Beat:</b> The mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. </div> </div> </div>And we add the following at the start or end of the Paradox Condition list to suit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abyssal Taint</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage has allowed another Paradox Condition to lapse. The Abyss has entered her Pattern, and appears in her Nimbus. Every spell she casts gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern. This deals a single point of lethal damage to the mage, and she does not gain Mana from the Scouring. She does not gain a Beat for resolving this Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-11-2017, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T02:28:08-08:00","id":1029971,"title":"","content":"^That's how I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}